%N A397114 Numbers of terms in A055932 that have the same prime signature as A025487(n).
%C A397114 Number of terms on n-th row of A096903.
%C A397114 We can calculate each term in terms of possible arrangements of the corresponding exponent vector. For example, A025487(55) = 2520 = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7, from which we have the exponent vector (3, 2, 1, 1) = [1^2, 2^1, 3^1], then a(55) = multinomial(4; 2,1,1) = 12.
%e A397114 a(13) = 3 because the 13th term in A025487 is 60, and there are 3 terms in A055932 that have the same prime signature as 60: 60, 90, and 150.
%Y A397114 Cf. A025487, A055932, A096903.
